"</Tabs>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Convenient construction methods {#convenient-construction-methods}"
msgstr "Méthodes de construction pratiques {#convenient-construction-methods}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For Python developers, several convenient construction methods are available that abstract away the sparse storage details. These make it easier to build operators without worrying about managing coefficient, mode, and boundary arrays:\n"
msgstr "Pour les développeurs Python, plusieurs méthodes de construction pratiques sont disponibles et masquent les détails du stockage creux. Elles facilitent la construction d'opérateurs sans avoir à gérer les tableaux de coefficients, de modes et de limites :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import FermionOperator, cre, ann\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Construct operators using operator algebra notation\n"
"    >>> op1 = FermionOperator.from_dict({(cre(0), ann(1)): 1.0})\n"
"    >>> op2 = FermionOperator.from_dict({(cre(2), ann(3)): 1.0})\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # The result is sparse even when combining them\n"
"    >>> op1 += op2\n"
"    >>> print(format(op1))\n"
"    1.000000e0 +0.000000e0j * (+0 -1)\n"
"    1.000000e0 +0.000000e0j * (+2 -3)\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    // The C API uses direct array construction; convenience methods are not available.\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hint\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Individual operator implementations might support additional construction methods suited to their specific use case. Check the API documentation for your operator type to see all available construction options.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Astuce\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Les implémentations individuelles d'opérateurs peuvent proposer des méthodes de construction supplémentaires adaptées à leur cas d'usage spécifique. Consulte la documentation de l'API de ton type d'opérateur pour voir toutes les options de construction disponibles.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

